{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואהבת", :translit "v'ahavta", :gloss "and you shall love"} {:he "אותיות האבות", :translit "otiot ha-avot", :gloss "letters of the patriarchs"} {:he "בכל לבבך", :translit "b'chol levavcha", :gloss "with all your heart"} {:he "כאברהם", :translit "k'avraham", :gloss "like Abraham"} {:he "ומצאת את לבבו", :translit "u'matzata et levavo", :gloss "and You found his heart"} {:he "ובכל נפשך", :translit "uv'chol nafsh'cha", :gloss "and with all your soul"} {:he "כיצחק", :translit "k'yitzchak", :gloss "like Isaac"} {:he "ובכל מאדך", :translit "uv'chol m'odecha", :gloss "and with all your might"} {:he "כיעקב", :translit "k'ya'akov", :gloss "like Jacob"} {:he "וכל אשר תתן לי עשר אעשרנו לך", :translit "v'chol asher titen li aser e'esrenu lach", :gloss "and all that You give me, I will surely tithe to You"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Notarikon proposed: the letters of ואהבת serve as an acronym for the three patriarchs, each corresponding to one of the three modes of love in the verse"}], :frame {:text "The three expressions of love in Deuteronomy 6:5 are each mapped to a patriarch: Abraham's heart was found faithful by God (Nehemiah 9:8, 'and You found his heart faithful before You'); Isaac surrendered his soul at the akedah (Genesis 22); and Jacob pledged to tithe all God would give him (Genesis 28:22). The reading 'with all your soul' as 'even if He takes your soul' is found at Berakhot 61b in the name of Rabbi Akiva. The association of each phrase with the respective patriarch appears in Sifrei Devarim 32.", :sources ["Genesis 22" "Genesis 28:22" "Nehemiah 9:8" "Sifrei Devarim 32" "Berakhot 61b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Notarikon proposed: the letters of ואהבת serve as an acronym for the three patriarchs, each corresponding to one of the three modes of love in the verse", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:48.086504417Z", :model "glm-5.2"}